$k>0$ is a constant of proportionality."] [:db/add "4f3f105f-8a0c-5397-99cc-b07c91edc702" :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the number of solar panels $P(t)$ installed changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum number of solar panels the facility can support and the current number of solar panels. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum number of solar panels the facility can support, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=156\\text{ panels},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(156-P).\n$$"] [:db/add "4f3f105f-8a0c-5397-99cc-b07c91edc702" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "4f3f105f-8a0c-5397-99cc-b07c91edc702" :question/answer-fields "8253f107-8fbb-5332-bcf7-662b2191ff63"] [:db/ensure "4f3f105f-8a0c-5397-99cc-b07c91edc702" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186124674 :knowledge-point/questions "4f3f105f-8a0c-5397-99cc-b07c91edc702"] [:db/add "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280" :answer/id #uuid "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280"] [:db/add "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280" :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(500-F)"] [:db/ensure "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280" :answer/validate] [:db/add "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac" :answer/id #uuid "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac"] [:db/add "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac" :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(F-232)"] [:db/ensure "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac" :answer/validate] [:db/add "62be25f4-6c92-5029-9fd7-2d48fc78b642" :answer/id #uuid "62be25f4-6c92-5029-9fd7-2d48fc78b642"] [:db/add "62be25f4-6c92-5029-9fd7-2d48fc78b642" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "62be25f4-6c92-5029-9fd7-2d48fc78b642" :answer/value "\\frac{\\text